{%- comment -%}
  "N+ sold" social proof. Added by EDD (Aug 2026).

  Usage: {% render 'units-sold', product: product %}
         {% render 'units-sold', product: product, variant: 'card' %}

  Reads product.metafields.custom.units_sold — an exact all-time count set from
  Shopify Analytics (inventory_units_sold). Nothing here queries orders; Liquid cannot,
  and a live count would be a page-load cost for a number that changes by single digits.

  Two rules, both deliberate:

  1. HIDDEN BELOW 100. The three books have sold 6,235 / 734 / 221. The jars are on 7 to
     20. "8 sold" is worse than saying nothing at all — it is the one number that talks a
     visitor out of buying. The threshold means the badge only ever appears where it helps.

  2. ROUNDED DOWN, NEVER UP. 6,235 shows as "6,000+", 734 as "700+". Rounding down keeps
     the claim true no matter how stale the metafield gets — the real figure only ever
     climbs past it — and a round number does not look like it was frozen on a date.

  Refresh: Analytics -> Reports, FROM inventory SHOW inventory_units_sold GROUP BY
  product_title, then update the metafield on each product. Quarterly is plenty.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign sold = product.metafields.custom.units_sold.value | plus: 0
  assign min_to_show = 100
-%}

{%- if sold >= min_to_show -%}
  {%- liquid
    if sold >= 1000
      assign thousands = sold | divided_by: 1000
      assign shown = thousands | append: ',000'
    else
      assign hundreds = sold | divided_by: 100 | times: 100
      assign shown = hundreds | append: ''
    endif
  -%}
  <p class="units-sold units-sold--{{ variant | default: 'card' }}">
    <svg class="units-sold__ico" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M5 7.5h14l-1.1 12.1a1.4 1.4 0 0 1-1.4 1.3H7.5a1.4 1.4 0 0 1-1.4-1.3L5 7.5Z"
            stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      <path d="M9 9.4V6.8a3 3 0 0 1 6 0v2.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    </svg>
    <span><strong>{{ shown }}+</strong> sold</span>
  </p>

  {%- style -%}
    .units-sold {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      margin: 6px 0 0;
      font-size: 12.5px;
      line-height: 1.3;
      color: #6B5744;
    }
    .units-sold strong {
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #2B1A0E;
    }
    /* A bag, not a heart: a heart on a product card reads as "wishlist", and this
       card already has a real wishlist control on the image. */
    .units-sold__ico {
      flex: none;
      width: 14px;
      height: 14px;
      color: #8A7A66;
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}
